WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:03.840
This video is a first walk through UM-Codex.

00:03.840 --> 00:07.940
You'll open its window, choose a folder, and watch Codex open on it.

00:07.940 --> 00:11.936
Then you'll ask Codex to do something, and stop and start again.

00:13.136 --> 00:17.556
Open UM-Codex from your Desktop, and its window opens in your browser.

00:17.556 --> 00:20.536
The first time, it shows a short Get started list.

00:20.536 --> 00:24.036
Your Toolkit key is saved, and Docker is running.

00:24.036 --> 00:26.296
Step three is Make your first setup.

00:26.296 --> 00:27.680
Press New setup.

00:28.180 --> 00:30.840
The form opens with everything already set.

00:30.840 --> 00:33.260
Under Folder, press Choose folder.

00:33.260 --> 00:38.044
At the bottom, What Codex gets says in plain words what the setup will allow.

00:38.544 --> 00:41.124
Choose the folder in your Mac's own folder picker.

00:41.124 --> 00:44.524
For this video, it's a demo folder of made-up files.

00:44.524 --> 00:49.728
For anything important, work in a copy, or in a folder that's a git repository.

00:50.228 --> 00:53.168
The rest is already set: the internet is on,

00:53.168 --> 00:56.608
the newest model, and Codex opens in the Codex app.

00:56.608 --> 00:59.708
Codex can change and delete files in that folder.

00:59.708 --> 01:02.568
They're your real files, with no undo.

01:02.568 --> 01:04.316
Press Save and start.

01:05.516 --> 01:06.736
That's all you do.

01:06.736 --> 01:10.016
The folder is now a setup, a card named after it.

01:10.016 --> 01:13.836
Its line goes from Starting, to Opening Codex, to Connected.

01:13.836 --> 01:18.316
UM-Codex opens its own copy of the Codex app, with its own settings.

01:18.316 --> 01:21.140
Your own ChatGPT app isn't touched.

01:21.640 --> 01:24.780
Codex opens on a project named after your folder.

01:24.780 --> 01:28.520
At the bottom, it says Remote, and the setup's name.

01:28.520 --> 01:31.760
That chat is running in the sealed environment on your Mac.

01:31.760 --> 01:36.664
A chat that doesn't say Remote would run on your Mac itself, so UM-Codex blocks it.

01:37.164 --> 01:39.604
Now ask Codex for something in the folder.

01:39.604 --> 01:43.804
Here, it summarizes the spreadsheet and writes a short note about it.

01:43.804 --> 01:48.684
Codex works inside the sealed environment, and the note lands in your real folder.

01:49.184 --> 01:52.184
Back in the window, the card has one summary line:

01:52.184 --> 01:56.324
the folder, where Codex opens, the internet, and the model.

01:56.324 --> 02:00.512
What Codex can do here opens the full list, in plain words.

02:01.712 --> 02:06.412
When you're finished, press Stop, at the top right of the card.

02:06.412 --> 02:06.452
It asks first.

02:06.452 --> 02:09.312
Codex stops and its sandbox is removed.

02:09.312 --> 02:14.132
Files it already changed in your folder stay as they are, and its history is kept.

02:14.132 --> 02:16.992
The Codex app then says it can't reconnect.

02:16.992 --> 02:18.320
That's expected.

02:18.820 --> 02:21.480
Next time, the same button says Start.

02:21.480 --> 02:22.500
One click.

02:22.500 --> 02:27.660
Under the card, Edit, Rename, Duplicate and Delete are small links.

02:27.660 --> 02:30.900
Edit shows three sections: Folder, Access and Codex.

02:30.900 --> 02:36.364
That's where you add a folder Codex can only read, or turn the internet off.

02:36.864 --> 02:38.424
That's your first launch.
